@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# K70 RAM 源码与候选实现
+
+`FdtRamPlan.c/.h` 是有界纯元数据解析器和范围规划器；`MeasuredRam.c/.h` 在已验证的输入映射之后执行受检查的 GCD 发布，实际被复制进相邻 boot05 的 DarwinBoot 编译。此目录不是另一个已验证的手机固件。
+
+[SOURCE-REVIEW.txt](SOURCE-REVIEW.txt) 与 [source-audit.json](source-audit.json) 记录了原厂 DTB、重新建立的 HOB 列表、OEM RamPartition ABI 和 SMEM 402 路径。原厂静态 DTB 以及叠加后的 DTB 均没有非零 RAM bank；OEM EnvDxe 还存在缺少真实表时的固定范围回退。因此 boot05 既没有恢复旧 BootMemoryDxe，也没有启用 OEM Scheduler/USB 链来猜测 RAM。
+
+`run-host-tests.py` 使用现有固定版本的 bundled libfdt，覆盖真实静态 DTB 的拒绝结果、1500 轮逐页集合对照和发布提交/失败状态模型。`check-window.py` 对实际 boot05 窗口头进行 600 轮暴力逐页参考比较。`check-boot05-coff.py` 使用真实 EDK 头编译新的两个 C 单元及完整 DarwinBoot C 单元。它们都是宿主验证，不能证明新 bank 在手机上的可访问性或系统启动。
+
+`prepare-boot05.py` 从已验证的本地 boot04 快照生成独立候选，默认拒绝覆盖不同内容；`--refresh-owned` 仅用于明确修改尚与之前所有权清单相符的文件，不能在正在构建或已冻结的运行时源码上使用。脚本依赖固定本地目录、原厂输入和既有构建结果，具体约定见相邻 boot05 README。
diff --git a/research/memory-next/SOURCE-REVIEW.txt b/research/memory-next/SOURCE-REVIEW.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d560162
--- /dev/null
+++ b/research/memory-next/SOURCE-REVIEW.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@
+K70 RAM extension source review, 2026-11-04
+
+Scope and handset evidence
+
+The parent agent reports that boot04 now actually enters XNU/bsd_init and
+stops at "failed to mount root device". Boot04's 128 MiB heap window is
+therefore useful as a preserved working baseline. This does not establish
+any other RAM bank, storage initialization, root mount or userland execution.
+The next memory candidate is boot-chain-05. No boot04 runtime file is changed.
+
+What the existing metadata does, and does not, establish
+
+1. Original stock-analysis/vendor_boot/dtb-002.dtb has /memory/reg containing
+   a zero address and zero length. The composed vermeer-v2 DTB (overlay 54)
+   still has no nonzero bank. The tested parser reports respectively 47 and
+   52 fixed reservations, but zero RAM banks. A reservation's complement is
+   not a measurement of usable RAM. The on-phone FDT may be filled by ABL;
+   its actual runtime contents have not yet been collected in this review.
+
+2. Mu-Silicium Sec.c InitializeMemory() calls HobConstructor at the known
+   DXE Heap and builds new memory HOBs from MemoryMapLib. The original XBL
+   resource HOB list is not handed through this code. BootShim preserves x0,
+   overwrites x1 with its payload address, and uses x2/x3 while copying. The
+   saved gSiliciumEntryArgHob contains the incoming Linux-style FDT address,
+   not an original EFI_SYSTEM_TABLE pointer or an original complete RAM map.
+
+3. Qcom PlatformPeiLib/PlatformPei.c BuildXblHobs() creates InfoBlk, Shim,
+   Prodmode, Scheduler, FV-list and DTB-extension HOBs. It does not import a
+   dynamic DDR partition table. Enabling PcdBuildXblHobs is consequently not
+   a RAM discovery fix. Boot05 leaves it FALSE and loads no new OEM chain.
+
+4. Exact OEM EnvDxe does publish EFI_RAMPARTITION_PROTOCOL GUID
+   5172ffb5-4253-7d51-c641-a701f973103c. In the pinned PE, installer RVA
+   24a0..24ec passes the GUID at e178 and protocol table at e290 to boot
+   services offset 148 (InstallMultipleProtocolInterfaces). The table has
+   revision 10002 and GetRamPartitions at RVA 2274. This is offline ABI
+   evidence; no protocol has been observed on boot04.
+
+5. That OEM implementation obtains SMEM item 0x192 (402), checks magic words
+   9da5e0a8 / af9ec4e2 and a nonzero table version (RVA 6d1c..6db4). There
+   are distinct version-1 and later table walks in 6f64..73e4. Critically,
+   when the item getter returns the unavailable status, 71e0..7248 builds a
+   hardcoded 80000000 + 60000000 range from constants c7a0/c7a8. A successful
+   higher-level protocol result alone is therefore not proof that this phone
+   supplied a real partition table. Boot05 does not call this implementation.
+
+6. Existing Qcom RamManagerLib depends on that protocol. Its count is UINT32
+   but returned via UINT8; the cached partition buffer is freed by the first
+   consumer. Generic RamManagerDxe also supplies NULL memory-map output
+   parameters and has an uninitialized MemoryRange cleanup path. Enabling
+   the whole existing path is not a small bounded replacement for the new
+   FDT reader. Neither it nor old VermeerBootMemoryDxe is added to boot05 FV.
+
+Concrete boot05 implementation
+
+The new helpers run inside the isolated DarwinBoot copy, after the preserved
+boot04 input-memory coverage/heap-overlap checks and before any kernel file
+allocation. K70ReadFdtRam first performs libfdt's bounded full check on the
+already readable FDT buffer, then collects only explicit nonzero memory/reg
+banks. It excludes the FDT reserve map, fixed reserved-memory/reg and complete
+alloc-ranges for dynamic reservations. An unknown dynamic reservation, malformed
+range, unsupported restrictive usable-memory property, excess count or integer
+overflow is refused. Disabled/hotplug memory is not silently added.
+
+K70PlanNewRam intersects those banks with the CURRENT GCD's NonExistent
+ranges, subtracts live FDT/initrd exclusions, checks physical-address bounds,
+and returns page-aligned ranges. Existing Reserved/SystemMemory/MMIO ranges
+are never reclassified, including the four boot04 uncertainty reservations.
+The publisher requires at least 514 MiB contiguous and publishes at most
+1 GiB. The extra 2 MiB guarantees room for any XNU physical/virtual phase.
+
+At commit, it raises TPL_NOTIFY, rechecks exact GCD ownership, installs a real
+WB CPU mapping using EFI_MEMORY_WB (not the ARM enum value 1), and only then
+calls AddMemorySpace(SystemMemory). AddMemorySpace is the commit point:
+DXE's CoreAddMemoryDescriptor may synchronously allocate from the new bank.
+After any failed/partial commit, the bank remains mapped, no blind removal or
+unmapping occurs, the loader returns a fixed failure reason and refuses any
+publication retry until firmware reboot. A later SetMemorySpaceAttributes
+failure follows the same rule. The ordinary menu remains available.
+
+The loader accepts only an explicit 512 MiB ADT request and allocates only
+within the successfully published range. It has no heap/hole/static-high-bank
+fallback. If runtime FDT still contains zero banks, or no eligible 514 MiB
+range remains, it must display M05 REFUSED and return to the menu.
+
+This is metadata-authorized normal RAM initialization, not a probe of arbitrary
+physical addresses. The pure parser/planner reads only its supplied FDT and
+range arrays. The publisher's page-table/GCD operations can access a new bank
+during normal firmware allocation; they do not prove accessibility in advance.
+Runtime metadata, XPU behavior, contiguous allocation and the resulting XNU
+memory budget still require an observed handset test of the complete image.
+
+Validation already completed
+
+- ASan/UBSan against the pinned bundled libfdt, real stock and composed DTBs.
+- 1500 randomized page-set comparisons for reservations and exclusions.
+- Publication-service model: ownership changes, premap failure, partial add,
+  post-commit attribute failure, ready-state reuse and missing bank rejection.
+- Real production EDK headers: AArch64 COFF for the two new C units and the
+  complete modified DarwinBoot.c. Entry.S remains byte-identical to boot04.
+- EDK genc/metadata completed successfully with 21 runtime files unchanged.
+
+The separate full EDK build and final FD/image audit have their own reports.
+Compilation, host models and FDT planning do not establish a working iPadOS OS.
+
+Build and final verification commands (WSL Ubuntu)
+
+python3.11 /mnt/e/K70-UniXNU-20261104/boot-chain-05/build.py
+python3.11 /mnt/e/K70-UniXNU-20261104/boot-chain-05/audit-fd.py
+python3.11 /mnt/e/K70-UniXNU-20261104/boot-chain-05/package.py
+
+Host-only source validation commands
+
+python3.11 /mnt/e/K70-UniXNU-20261104/memory-next/run-host-tests.py
+python3.11 /mnt/e/K70-UniXNU-20261104/memory-next/check-boot05-coff.py
+
+Do not rerun prepare-boot05.py --refresh-owned during an active build. Its
+refresh mode only replaces files still matching its prior owned-source audit;
+it is for an intentional new source revision, not for changing a frozen build.
diff --git a/research/memory-next/add-durable-stop.py b/research/memory-next/add-durable-stop.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8722131
--- /dev/null
+++ b/research/memory-next/add-durable-stop.py
@@ -0,0 +1,171 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Preserve verified boot05, add only durable error UI, keep RAM logic unchanged."""
+import hashlib
+import json
+from pathlib import Path
+import shutil
+
+HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
+WORK = HERE.parent/'boot-chain-05'
+DRIVER = WORK/'darwinboot/DarwinBootPkg/Driver'
+build = json.loads((WORK/'build-result.json').read_text())
+audit = json.loads((WORK/'fd-audit.json').read_text())
+assert build['exit_code'] == 0 and not build['source_changed_during_build']
+assert audit['success'] and audit['fd_sha256'] == '2d207ced094daee8b72c22029efc64b54f37021546af1c1663a0614ee4a164fc'
+snapshot = WORK/'source-snapshots/initial-verified-2d207ced'
+assert not snapshot.exists(), 'Original snapshot already exists; do not reapply blindly'
+for name, digest in build['source_sha256'].items():
+    data = (WORK/name).read_bytes()
+    assert hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest() == digest, name
+    target = snapshot/name;target.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);target.write_bytes(data)
+for name in ('build-result.json','fd-audit.json','build.log','coff-check.json','window-check.json','preparation-audit.json'):
+    shutil.copyfile(WORK/name,snapshot/name)
+shutil.copyfile(HERE.parent/'artifacts/boot-chain-05/verification.json',snapshot/'verification.json')
+shutil.copyfile(WORK/'build.py',snapshot/'build.py')
+shutil.copyfile(WORK/'package.py',snapshot/'package.py')
+
+def once(text, old, new):
+    assert text.count(old)==1, old
+    return text.replace(old,new)
+
+p=DRIVER/'DarwinBoot.c';source=p.read_text()
+assert 'K70HoldFailure' not in source
+source=once(source,'STATIC K70_RAM_RANGE mMeasuredWindow;', '''STATIC K70_RAM_RANGE mMeasuredWindow;
+STATIC BOOLEAN mFailureHeld;
+STATIC CONST VOID *mValidatedFdt;
+STATIC UINTN mValidatedFdtBytes;''')
+needle='STATIC\nEFI_STATUS\nK70CheckEntryInputs (VOID);'
+helper='''// Keep a failure visible inside the loader until the user releases the old
+// selection key and presses a new key. The menu cannot redraw over this screen
+// until this function returns. These diagnostics do not publish or retry RAM.
+STATIC
+VOID
+K70HoldFailure (CONST CHAR16 *Detail, EFI_STATUS Failure)
+{
+  EFI_INPUT_KEY Key;
+  EFI_STATUS KeyStatus;
+  UINTN Quiet = 0;
+  BOOLEAN Armed = FALSE;
+  CHAR16 Line[160];
+  K70_FDT_RAM Meta;
+  int MetaResult;
+
+  if (mFailureHeld) { return; }
+  mFailureHeld = TRUE;
+  if (gST->ConOut != NULL && gST->ConOut->ClearScreen != NULL) {
+    gST->ConOut->ClearScreen (gST->ConOut);
+  }
+  Print (L"\\nK70 BOOT05R1 STOP: %s\\nStatus: %r\\n", Detail, Failure);
+  DiagDraw (L"K70 BOOT05R1 - FAILURE HELD", 0);
+  DiagDraw (Detail, 1);
+  UnicodeSPrint (Line, sizeof (Line), L"STATUS %r (0x%lx)", Failure, (UINT64)Failure);
+  DiagDraw (Line, 4);
+  if (mValidatedFdt != NULL && mValidatedFdtBytes >= 40) {
+    MetaResult = K70ReadFdtRam (mValidatedFdt, mValidatedFdtBytes, &Meta);
+    UnicodeSPrint (Line, sizeof (Line), L"META %d BANKS %u RESV %u DYN %u",
+                   MetaResult, Meta.BankCount, Meta.ReservedCount, Meta.DynamicReservationUnknown);
+    DiagDraw (Line, 6);
+    UnicodeSPrint (Line, sizeof (Line), L"FDT PA %lx BYTES %lx",
+                   (UINT64)(UINTN)mValidatedFdt, (UINT64)mValidatedFdtBytes);
+    DiagDraw (Line, 8);
+  }
+  DiagDraw (L"RELEASE KEYS; PRESS AGAIN FOR MENU", 10);
+  DiagDraw (L"KEEP THIS SCREEN TO REPORT THE REASON", 11);
+  // The only metadata re-read above is the already coverage-validated FDT.
+  // No candidate RAM address is read or written by the failure screen.
+  for (;;) {
+    ZeroMem (&Key, sizeof (Key));
+    KeyStatus = EFI_NOT_READY;
+    if (gST->ConIn != NULL && gST->ConIn->ReadKeyStroke != NULL) {
+      KeyStatus = gST->ConIn->ReadKeyStroke (gST->ConIn, &Key);
+    }
+    if (!EFI_ERROR (KeyStatus) && (Key.ScanCode != 0 || Key.UnicodeChar != 0)) {
+      if (Armed) { return; }
+      Quiet = 0;
+    } else if (!Armed && ++Quiet >= 40) {
+      Armed = TRUE;
+    }
+    // One quiet second drains held-key repeats before a fresh key is accepted.
+    // Missing console input leaves the reason visible for hardware reboot.
+    gBS->Stall (25000);
+  }
+}
+
